	(310, 'During the tour the icebreaker had its regular maintenance at the dock. Its engines are turned off. Diesel generators provide the power.', '002.jpg', 1, 16),
	(311, 'The ship is located in No. 3 dock of the ship-repairing plant in Murmansk.', '003.jpg', 2, 16),
	(312, 'The breathtaking view! When you see it, you immediately get the way it works. This huge ship crashes the ice with its massive body which has a specific shape. A part of the icebreaker is covered with the stainless steel to prevent the scratches and corrosion.', '004.jpg', 3, 16),
	(313, 'There is a system that provides powerful air streams. It helps to reduce the friction of the icebreaker\'s keel on the ice. It is simple:', '005.jpg', 4, 16),
	(314, 'The vessel is elevated due to its body maintenance. The workers are checking and fixing its rudder system. There are pictures of the propellers and rudders. Victory has 7 impressive and massive propellers which may be repaired during the sailing.', '006.jpg', 5, 16),
	(315, '', '007.jpg', 6, 16),
	(316, '"50 Let Pobedy" is the largest icebreaker in the world. Its length is 159,6 meters (521.65 feet), width is 30 meters (98 feet ), it is 17,2 meters high (56 feet), and its draft is about 11 meters (36 feet). Impressive, is not it?', '008.jpg', 7, 16),
	(317, 'The only way to reach the ship in the dock is this gangway. Let\'s get to the ship!', '009.jpg', 8, 16),
	(318, 'This is the ship\'s scheme. It has 14 levels and 1,300 rooms.', 'deck_plan.jpg', 9, 16),
	(319, 'First of all we visited the chief petty officers\' mess. There are two crews at the icebreaker, and each one works for four months. The captain met us very kindly, and we shake hands!', '011.jpg', 10, 16),
	(320, 'There are flowers in each room. Lots of good-looking flowers far from the sun, it is amazing!', '012.jpg', 11, 16),
	(321, 'We are talking in a very friendly manner, as we are friends for a long time. We asked questions and got the answers, and we had a delicious home-cooked meal.', '013.jpg', 12, 16),
	(322, 'The main gangway starts right here and leads up to the third bridge. Two more gangways connect the third and the fourth bridges. The walls are decorated with the pictures of modern and old-style icebreakers.', '014.jpg', 13, 16),
	(323, 'orridors, doors of cabins (on the right) and service rooms (on the left).', '015.jpg', 14, 16),
	(324, 'The ship is equipped with large and small gangways. One may get lost without a scheme in his or her hands.', '016.jpg', 15, 16),
	(325, 'The captain\'s cabin is very cozy and spacious, and it is very different from a cabin on a river vessel. Check out the wallpaper at the captain\'s computer with a view at the ship\'s prow!', '017.jpg', 16, 16),
	(326, 'The press-conference was held in the conference-hall next to the captain\'s room.', '018.jpg', 17, 16),
	(327, 'The gangway leads to the pilot room at the fourth level. The stunning view at the port!', '019.jpg', 18, 16),
	(328, 'Three persons are responsible for navigation of the icebreaker at a time, and every ship control watch lasts for four hours.', '020.jpg', 19, 16),
	(329, 'There are two pairs of the bridge equipment for safety and a lot of navigational equipment as well.', '021.jpg', 20, 16),
	(330, 'This is the main navigation bridge of the "50 Let Pobedy". This small steering wheel rotates the huge wheel pistons, and pistons rotate the giant heavy wheels that are responsible for the ship\'s direction.', '022.jpg', 21, 16),
	(331, 'The icebreaker is filled once a five year. This is a picture of the engine room was made by <span class="ljuser  i-ljuser  i-ljuser-type-P     " lj:user="sergeydolya"><a class="i-ljuser-username" href="http://sergeydolya.livejournal.com/" target="_self"><b>sergeydolya</b></a></span>:', '024.jpg', 22, 16),
	(332, 'At the middle bridge there are a cook room and a food storage.', '025.jpg', 23, 16),
	(333, 'The storage is huge and divided into sections for different purposes.', '026.jpg', 24, 16),
	(334, '', '027.jpg', 25, 16),
	(335, 'Phones are located all over the ship.', '028.jpg', 26, 16),
	(336, 'There are on-board entertainment rooms, a fitness center, a library, a sauna, a pool, bars, etc.', '029.jpg', 27, 16),
	(337, '', '030.jpg', 28, 16),
	(338, 'The fitness center.', '031.jpg', 29, 16),
	(339, 'The sauna and the pool with the ocean\'s water.', '032.jpg', 30, 16),
	(340, 'he vessel "50 Let Pobedy" is 10 meters long then other nuclear icebreakers. It has the modernized biological shielding complex and an ecological compartment.', '033.jpg', 31, 16),
	(341, 'The night illumination.', '034.jpg', 32, 16),
	(342, '', '001.jpg', 1, 17),
	(343, '', '002.jpg', 2, 17),
	(344, 'Fountains are switched-off.', '003.jpg', 3, 17),
	(345, '', '004.jpg', 4, 17),
	(346, 'Peter first made the decision to erect the residence, a triumphal monument, in honour of the victory in the Great Northern War which took place in 1700 to 1721.', '005.jpg', 5, 17),
	(347, 'triumph is in the design of all the fountains, but most of all it is in the central one, named Samson wrestling the jaws of a lion.', '006.jpg', 6, 17),
	(348, 'It was constructed in 1735 in honour of the 25 anniversary of the Poltava battle. The lion was chosen on purpose. Being a part of the Switzerland coat of arms it symbolizes the defeat. The fountain is the highest in Peterhof.', '007.jpg', 7, 17),
	(349, '', '008.jpg', 8, 17),
	(350, 'The Samson fountain uses 70 litres of water a second. Do the fountains operate with pumps? No! The answer is in the grotto.', '009.jpg', 9, 17),
	(351, 'The fountain\'s constructors faced a water problem. Pumps were very expensive. For that reason Peter first came up with an idea of supplying water by a gravity-led system.', '010.jpg', 10, 17),
	(352, 'The idea was used in the water-supply system of the fountains. A twenty-four kilometers long channel was built. It connects the lakes of Peterhof and its fountains.', '011.jpg', 11, 17),
	(353, 'The maintenance of the hydrotechnical system is done by a team of twenty-four professionals in the summer and 10 specialists in the winter. Peterhof\'s fountains are operated manually since the 18th century. Those tubes are have being used since the 19th century.', '012.jpg', 12, 17),
	(354, 'The bright coloring of the tubes helped 10 years old boys who worked here in the 18th century to recognize each one. For example the green tube brings water to the western fountains, the blue one to the Basket Fountain, the red one to the Samson fountain.', '013.jpg', 13, 17),
	(355, 'The heart of the Grand Cascade is the Lower Grotte with cascades made of the Pudist limestone. Its largest monument represents Faunus, the god of the forest and fields. In the center of the hall there is a dining table served with delicious meals, and when Peter\'s guests were about to get some fruits...', '014.jpg', 14, 17),
	(356, '...the Joke Fountain suddenly turned on! Its water streams rose up to two meters. This was the way Peter the Great made jokes on his guests. All of them were wet after visiting the Grotte.', '015.jpg', 15, 17),
	(357, 'There were no move sensors in the 18th century, and the greatest secret of those Joke Fountains is easy as a pie. They have being operating manually for almost four centuries. A guardian of the park turns them on now a days.', '016.jpg', 16, 17),
	(358, 'Some more pictures of the Lower waterfalls\' area.', '017.jpg', 17, 17),
	(359, '', '018.jpg', 18, 17),
	(360, '', '019.jpg', 19, 17),
	(361, 'The Basket Fountain.', '020.jpg', 20, 17),
	(362, 'Some pictures of the park.', '021.jpg', 21, 17),
	(363, '', '022.jpg', 22, 17),
	(364, '', '023.jpg', 23, 17),
	(365, '', '024.jpg', 24, 17),
	(366, '', '025.jpg', 25, 17),
	(367, 'A pretty abandoned waterfall.', '026.jpg', 26, 17),
	(368, '', '027.jpg', 27, 17),
	(369, '', '028.jpg', 28, 17),
	(370, '', '029.jpg', 29, 17),
	(371, 'A tip for tourists. The easiest way to get to Peterhof is to use the Meteor boats. The author of the review used Astra-Martin boats, and the trip took about half an hour.', '030.jpg', 30, 17),
	(372, '', '031.jpg', 31, 17),
	(373, '', '032.jpg', 32, 17),
	(374, '', '033.jpg', 33, 17),
	(375, '', '034.jpg', 34, 17),
	(376, 'Let\'s start our journey with Elektrozavodskaya station. It was opened on the 15 of May 1944. It would be an ordinary station, if not for its 318 stunning lightings! They are amazing!', '002.jpg', 1, 18),
	(377, 'The next stop on the blue line is the station Ploshchad Revolyutsii, which was opened in March 13 1938. It is very famous for the sculpture of a frontier guard with a dog. If you will rub the dog\'s nose, it will bring you luck. The legend is very popular, so the nose is polished very well.', '003.jpg', 2, 18),
	(378, 'Other statues, such as the golden chicken, the flag of a signalman and the revolver of a sailorman are also very popular. Olimpy Rudakov, the student of a Naval Academy, posed for the second statue. Later, in 1953, he danced the waltz with the Queen Elizabeth the II on the day of her coronation.', '004.jpg', 3, 18),
	(379, 'Arbatskaya station was opened on April 5 1953. Earlier the line Ploshchad Revolutsii – Kievskaya lied higher, but since the bomb had destroyed it, the line was rebuilt deeper in the ground. In 1976 a musical video of famous Russian singer Alla Pugacheva was filmed here.', '005.jpg', 4, 18),
	(380, 'The last station on this line that is worth to be mentioned is Slavyansky Bulvar. This is one of the most beautiful stations that were opened in the 21 century, it is the second breath of the underground architecture! It was opened on the 7th of September 2008.', '006.jpg', 5, 18),
	(381, '', '007.jpg', 6, 18),
	(382, '', '008.jpg', 7, 18),
	(383, 'Now let\'s change the line. You may find a beauty even in its interchanges if it is not a rush-hour.', '009.jpg', 8, 18),
	(384, 'Well, it is a matter of taste, but I like Trubnaya station, which is also relatively new. It was opened on August 30 2007. Its stained glasses are decorated with pictures of churches and cathedrals, which were painted with out сrosses on its domes. Passengers have tacked small crosses to the pictures by themselves.', '010.jpg', 9, 18),
	(385, '', '011.jpg', 10, 18),
	(386, 'Well, you must be surprised with a picture of a plain station Rimskaya. I lived next to this station and I like the photo.', '012.jpg', 11, 18),
	(387, 'Now we will move to the Koltsevaya line with the most beautiful stations, which keep a lot of secrets and stories. Here is one of them. According to the documents, Joseph Stalin ordered to base the Moscow subway on an astrologic map of the sorcerer Jacov Bruice. For that reason there are 12 stations on the Koltsevaya line, since there are 12 Zodiac Signs. Station Prospect Mira was opened on January 30 1952.', '013.jpg', 12, 18),
	(388, 'Komsomolskaya station is an apotheosis of the Stalin\'s empire style. It should have been the busiest in the city, and function as Moscow\'s gates. So it was a grandiose building. Komsomolskaya was to amaze tourists, who visited the Soviet Union\'s capital. It was constructed by A. V. Shchusev and opened on January 30 1952.', '014.jpg', 13, 18),
	(389, 'Now we will move to Kievskaya station, which was opened on March 14 1954. By the way, if the train moves in a clockwise direction, a man\'s voice announces stations. If it moves in a contraclockwise direction, you will hear a woman\'s voice. It helps visually impaired passangers to orientate.', '015.jpg', 14, 18),
	(390, 'Both Kievskaya stations, on the Koltsevaya and Radialnaya lines, are incredible beautiful.', '016.jpg', 15, 18),
	(391, 'Nikita Khrushchev did not like the projects of those stations in 1953, and architects had to redo them. The station was opened on April 5 1953.', '017.jpg', 16, 18),
	(392, 'In the morning of October 2 2010 the fresco "Selebration in Kiev" has crashed, and it took three years to restore it.', '018.jpg', 17, 18),
	(393, 'The most beautiful station on the Koltsevaya line, Novoslobodskaya, which was opened on January 30 1952.', '019.jpg', 18, 18),
	(394, 'It was planned to make its stained glasses of uranium glass. But they were made of a colored glass by Latvian artists.', '020.jpg', 19, 18),
	(395, 'Architects have created a station-grotto with a mild illumination.', '021.jpg', 20, 18),
	(396, 'The first place goes to Mayakovskaya station, which was opened on September 11 1938. It is not grandiose, but in my opinion this station is the most beautiful. I have never seen such an amazing interior.', '022.jpg', 21, 18),
	(397, 'It is decorated with a panel at the top.', '023.jpg', 22, 18),
	(398, 'The project won the grand prize at the New York world fair in 1938. It was a shelter during the Great Patriotic War.', '024.jpg', 23, 18),
	(399, '', '001.jpg', 1, 19),
	(400, 'That day we had our breakfast in a raw-hide tent. We are entering the raw-hide tent.', '002.jpg', 2, 19),
	(401, 'We were sitting here. An oven, which was used for cooking and warming-up, was in the center. It was warm in front of it but a little cold behind the oven.', '003.jpg', 3, 19),
	(402, 'We had a traditional meal, which consists of meat and dough in broth. There is no pasta or macaroni in Taiga.', '004.jpg', 4, 19),
	(403, 'There were a lot of kids here. All of they are studying in a local boarding school.', '005.jpg', 5, 19),
	(404, 'Everyone had a chance to have a ride in a reindeer sleigh.', '006.jpg', 6, 19),
	(405, 'A market near the central scene of the celebration. They sold clothes of fur and leather, berries, nuts, meat, souvenirs, etc. I was surprised to see raspberries here!', '007.jpg', 7, 19),
	(406, '', '008.jpg', 8, 19),
	(407, 'I have never seen so many deer.', '009.jpg', 9, 19),
	(408, 'White deer stuck out.', '010.jpg', 10, 19),
	(409, 'It is always nice to meet husky. Beautiful dogs!', '011.jpg', 11, 19),
	(410, 'I liked those dolls without faces. A doll with a face is a bad sign. They believe that the evil spirit may get into a doll with a face.', '012.jpg', 12, 19),
	(411, 'The central entertainment of the celebration is a race with a great prize, a snowmobile Buran. Sometimes reindeer sleigh ran into each other.', '013.jpg', 13, 19),
	(412, '', '014.jpg', 14, 19),
	(413, '', '015.jpg', 15, 19),
	(414, '', '016.jpg', 16, 19),
	(415, 'A mess at the hot contest.', '017.jpg', 17, 19),
	(416, 'This reindeer sleigh was the first, but there is no woman in it.', '018.jpg', 18, 19),
	(417, 'She reached the finish line later.', '019.jpg', 19, 19),
	(418, 'Deer saw bloggers at the finish, got afraid and stopped three meters before the finish line.', '020.jpg', 20, 19),
	(419, 'Happy end. Winners crossed the finish line on feet. At the picture is the second finalist.', '021.jpg', 21, 19),
	(420, 'Here is the owner of deer, which crossed the finish line alone.', '022.jpg', 22, 19),
	(421, '', '023.jpg', 23, 19),
	(422, 'The winner told us that she won the competition in the previous year as well.', '024.jpg', 24, 19),
	(423, 'Women at the start.', '025.jpg', 25, 19),
	(424, '', '026.jpg', 26, 19),
	(425, 'An unusual sports.', '027.jpg', 27, 19),
	(426, 'A small tragedy at the men\'s finish. The winner stumbled, then...', '028.jpg', 28, 19),
	(427, '...fall and lost.', '029.jpg', 29, 19),
	(428, 'Women\'s finish.', '030.jpg', 30, 19),
	(429, 'I would like to thank those, who organized the celebration for the warm clothes and shoes that we got. We would not be able to make pictures without it! I would get cold in half an hour my own winter clothes, because it was windy. Those competitions were sponsored by authorities of Surgut\'s region.', '031.jpg', 31, 19),
	(430, 'A beautiful soaring of skydivers.', '032.jpg', 32, 19),
	(431, '', '033.jpg', 33, 19),
	(432, 'One more competition Throwing of Lasso.', '034.jpg', 34, 19),
	(433, '', '035.jpg', 35, 19),
	(434, 'The loop becomes wider as it falls on the ground, and this one got even me.', '036.jpg', 36, 19),
	(435, '', '037.jpg', 37, 19),
	(436, '', '001.jpg', 1, 20),
	(437, 'In 10 to 11 centuries several messuages were located at the territory of the future Kremlin. The Prince Vladimir Yaroslavovich, the son of Jaroslav Mudry, started the building of the wooden Detinets. The Sophiyskaya Church, the main temple of the Kremlin, was built in 1045-1052. It was sanctified in 1052, and seven months later the Prince Vladimir died. He was buried in the Church.', '002.jpg', 2, 20),
	(438, '', '003.jpg', 3, 20),
	(439, '', '004.jpg', 4, 20),
	(440, '', '005.jpg', 5, 20),
	(441, '', '006.jpg', 6, 20),
	(442, 'In 1065 the wooden Kremlin was attacked by the Prince of Polotsk, Vyacheslav Bryatislavovich. The fortress of the 11th century had only two gates. Two roads lead to those gates, Velikaya Street of Nerevsk end and Priboynaya Street of Ludin end. Piskuplya Street was the main street in the Kremlin.', '007.jpg', 7, 20),
	(443, '', '008.jpg', 8, 20),
	(444, '', '009.jpg', 9, 20),
	(445, '', '010.jpg', 10, 20),
	(446, '', '011.jpg', 11, 20),
	(447, 'In the middle of the 11th century two more parts, the North-Eastern and Southern, were built, and Kremlin became larger. In 1097 the wooden Detinets burned out. The fortress was rebuilt much later, in 1116. In 1136 the Prince\'s power was limited by veche. Princes moved to Gorodische, and Kremlin became a residence for new leaders, Novgorod\'s supreme state authority. A significant part of Detinets was occupied by archbishop. His residence, Vladychny Dvor, was built with numerous churches, rwsidential buildings and household facilities. Unfortunately, Detinets\' walls burned out again and were rebuilt in 1262. Later, in 1333, archbishop Vasily (Kalika) started building of a new Detinets of stone. The tough fortress was to protect Novgorod of an army of Ivan Kalita and Swedish troops. The stone Detinets was ready in 30s of the 15th century. Later, in 1348, Sweds broke the peaceful agreement, attacked Novgorod\'s lands and captured Votskaya Pyatina and the fortress Orekhov. For that reason building of Detinets was postponed up to the 50s of the 15th century.</p>', '012.jpg', 12, 20),
	(448, '', '013.jpg', 13, 20),
	(449, '', '014.jpg', 14, 20),
	(450, '', '015.jpg', 15, 20),
	(451, '', '016.jpg', 16, 20),
	(452, 'The fortress was totally rebuilt in 1478 to 1490 in the time of the Great Prince Ivan the third. On May 7 1862 a big peace of a wall, that was rebuilt two years before, was ruined. It was erected again, became thinner and had deep niches in it. Part of the new wall had some rooms in it, which were used as a historical archive. In 1941 to 1944 those rooms were used by German troops. On April 30 1991 a part of the wall near the Spasskaya Tower was ruined again. It was restored in 1994 to 1996.', '017.jpg', 17, 20),
	(453, '', '018.jpg', 18, 20),
	(454, '', '019.jpg', 19, 20),
	(455, '', '020.jpg', 20, 20),
	(456, '', '021.jpg', 21, 20),
	(457, 'Detinets stands on a ten meter high hill and has a shape similar to oval. The perimeter of its walls is 1487 meters. The longest wall is 565 meters long, and its territory is 12.1 hectares. Walls and Towers of Detinets. Its walls are built with sand-lime bricks. Kremlin\'s stone laying consists of lime and cobblestone. Its walls are 3.6 to 6.5 meters thick and 8 to 15 meters high. The fortress has several churches over-the-gates. Novgorod bishops initiated the building of those churches. Most of walls, which were restored in 1950s to 1960s, have the style of the 15th century.', '022.jpg', 22, 20),
	(458, '', '023.jpg', 23, 20),
	(459, '', '024.jpg', 24, 20),
	(460, '', '025.jpg', 25, 20),
	(461, '', '026.jpg', 26, 20),
	(462, '', '027.jpg', 27, 20),
	(463, '', '028.jpg', 28, 20),
	(464, 'Some of the Kremlin\'s towers names are not historical. For instance, names Dvortsovaya, Knyazhaya and Kokuy were created in 19th to 20th centuries. Each tower had five or six levels inside. Those levels were connected with wooden stairs. Lower levels were often used as a storage for ammunition. Moreover, towers were equipped with elevating systems for weapons.', '029.jpg', 29, 20),
	(465, '', '030.jpg', 30, 20),
	(466, '', '031.jpg', 31, 20),
	(467, '', '032.jpg', 32, 20),
	(468, '', '033.jpg', 33, 20),
	(469, '', '001.jpg', 1, 21),
	(470, 'It is sterile clean here. We were asked to put on a uniform so as to protect plants.', '002.jpg', 2, 21),
	(471, 'The first impression of the place is that we got into a futuristic factory! It is 6 meters (19,6 feet) high. There are a lot of sensors, control panels and 700 kilometers (435 miles) of heating tubes. The modern greenhouse facility is automized, so the number of workers in it is very low. We will talk about the personnel and control systems a little later.', '003.jpg', 3, 21),
	(472, 'Let\'s have a look at the automatic sowing line. It is the beginning of the process of growing.', '004.jpg', 4, 21),
	(473, 'The machine is 12-15 times faster than a gang of 4 workers. At the picture you can see how it sucks up the seeds. After that the seeds are automatically planted into the planting pots, which are also prepared by the machine.', '005.jpg', 5, 21),
	(474, 'You can see the result of the line\'s work. Each pot, filled with a coconut substrate, has three seeds in it. A seed coating is a process of covering seeds with a protective coat, and it is a part of a presowing treatment.', '006.jpg', 6, 21),
	(475, 'The next step. Trays with "fertilized" pots are placed in a cell with suitable temperature and humidity for greensprouting.', '007.jpg', 7, 21),
	(476, 'After that trays are transported to the seeding room, which is illuminated 24x7. They will sit here for ten days.', '008.jpg', 8, 21),
	(477, 'Tables with plastic trays and a specific solution feed system. The solution washes the plant\'s roots for fifteen minutes, and then gets back into the system.', '009.jpg', 9, 21),
	(478, 'All those tables are easy to move, and it helps to save the extremely expensive space in the room.', '010.jpg', 10, 21),
	(479, 'Guess, what are those yellow leaves used for? From time to time insects may fly into this hermetic facility, and those yellow things help to kill them. A solution circulates in those white rectangle channels and washes the plant\'s roots. After twenty days all mature produce will be packed and transported to stores. The facility produces up to four thousand pieces of salad a day.', '011.jpg', 11, 21),
	(480, 'Pay your attention to the number of lamps at the ceiling. The facility must be properly lightened all over the day.', '012.jpg', 12, 21),
	(481, 'An expensive energy has always been a serious problem for modern companies. The facility has no gas, and for that reason the company had to build its own powerful energy substation. It will be launched soon.', '013.jpg', 13, 21),
	(482, 'Here the solution with a given level of EC and pH is prepared of water, mother solution and citric. The computer is controlling the process to prevent mistakes.', '014.jpg', 14, 21),
	(483, 'A user-friendly interface of the watering system is easy to learn and use.', '015.jp', 15, 21),
	(484, 'It seems to me that we have spent a lot of time in this room. Let\'s move forward to the section with tomatoes. It\'s area is two hectares. The real tomato jungles, which are higher than a human! The section with cucumbers is equal to the tomatoes\'.', '016.jpg', 16, 21),
	(485, 'The area is equipped with a system of drip watering. It means that every of 350,000 plants has its own dropper. You can see those small tubes at the roots.', '017.jpg', 17, 21),
	(486, 'Talking about women. Men do not do well at this job, even though it seems to be an easy one. Moreover, it is very difficult to find a qualified staff, despite the fact that they are paid well.', '018.jpg', 18, 21),
	(487, 'In a greenhouse facility tomatoes grow up to 14 meters high (46 feet), and women put them on specific bandings. Thin plastic tubes with small holes are everywhere. Those tubes bring carbon dioxide to the plants. Its concentration is absolutely safe for people.', '019.jpg', 19, 21),
	(488, 'Since those cucumbers are pollinated by bees, there is a beekeeping at the facility. Bees are transported from Uzbekistan because they wake up earlier then Russian bees. Thus, they began pollinating earlier, in January or February.', '020.jpg', 20, 21),
	(489, 'Sergey and Nikita are waiting to make a picture of bumblebee, and Nikita even knocks at their cardboard house. I prefer to stay away from them.', '023.jpg', 21, 21),
	(490, 'The picture of ripening tomatoes. Let\'s move to cucumbers.', '024.jpg', 22, 21),
	(491, 'Tomatoes are planted once a year, cucumbers – twice: November through June and July – November.', '025.jpg', 23, 21),
	(492, 'As you can see, those cucumbers have pimples. My mom and wife buy the same.', '026.jp', 24, 21),
	(493, 'There is a biological laboratory, which produces mites. Those are used to fight pests and are not dangerous for people.', '027.jpg', 25, 21),
	(494, 'And finally a picture of a screenshot with interface of the control program Monitor. It allocates information and provides monitoring of all processes at the facility. The program helps to analyze allocated information and inform its user about problems.', '028.jpg', 26, 21),
	(495, 'For the moment there are nine jets in the workshop. You can see six, other three are hiding over the wall.', '001.jpg', 1, 22),
	(496, 'For comparison this is the workshop in 2006. A poster that says "RRJ will become alive here" is on the wall. RRJ, or Russian Regional Jet, is the first name of Sukhoi Superjet. Rebranding took place at the Farnborough International Airshow in 2006.', '002.jpg', 2, 22),
	(497, 'A part of the aiplane\'s fuselage.', '003.jpg', 3, 22),
	(498, 'The first assembled airplane had the number 95002. The first machine N 95001 is for flights, the second one, 95002, is for ground tests. The airplane N95002 was assembled first for all tests and red tapes. On the January 28 2007 the airplane was transported in the airplane Ruslan to TSAGI for tests, which took a few years.', '004.jpg', 4, 22),
	(499, 'In July 2007 the jet 95001 was demonstrated to journalists for the third time. After this the airplane gets its wings, and vortex generators, in September of 2007 it is ready for the final presentation.', '005.jpg', 5, 22),
	(500, 'The fourth tour to Komsomolsk-na-Amure, the demonstration of the Superjet is on the 26 of September 2007.', '006.jpg', 6, 22),
	(501, 'On the first day the airplane demonstrated taxiing. On the second day we saw its chassis tests. Finally, on the last day, May 19, 2008, Superjet number 95001 got off the ground!', '007.jpg', 7, 22),
	(502, 'The airplane number 95036 is assembled for a Mexican company Interjet, which has placed an order for 20 machines.', '008.jpg', 8, 22),
	(503, 'The final part of assembly in the workshop.', '009.jpg', 9, 22),
	(504, 'Fuselage is manufactured in Komsomolsk, the cabin and tail – in Novosibirsk, the engine in Rybinsk.', '010.jpg', 10, 22),
	(505, 'At the section number one there is an airplane number 95029 for the Airflot company.', '011.jpg', 11, 22),
	(506, 'Installation of cables and avionics.', '012.jpg', 12, 22),
	(507, 'Installation of cable in the cabin. This delicate work is for women.', '013.jpg', 13, 22),
	(508, 'Check of cords with specific devices. There are areas, where it is impossible to install sealed cords. In this case some cords are sealed at the board of an airplane. At the picture: cords checking after its sealing. After that all systems are energized and tested.', '014.jpg', 14, 22),
	(509, 'The red light is on. Everything is ok!', '015.jpg', 15, 22),
	(510, 'The length of all cords in the airplane is 10 kilometers (6.2 miles)!', '016.jpg', 16, 22),
	(511, 'Airplane\'s serial number changes when machines are passed to customers.', '017.jpg', 17, 22),
	(512, 'Installation of an air stairs light.', '018.jpg', 18, 22),
	(513, 'Installation of slats\' components.', '019.jpg', 19, 22),
